her see a cheap river or get the other player to make a move.\n\n\n", 'output': "Evaluation: You hold a pair of 4s and a gutshot straight draw (needing a 5) on a board of 3-J-4-2. The opponent has shown weakness by checking pre-flop and on the flop. However, your hand is marginal (low pair), and building a large pot is risky given you are out of position. Checking allows you to potentially see the river card for free, realizing your equity without inflating the pot.\n\nReason: You have a made hand with showdown value (pair of 4s) and a straight draw. Checking is the safest option to control the pot size and keep opponent's range wide. Betting might force out worse hands while only getting action from better hands (like a Jack or higher pair).\n\nAnswer: 0"}
