assivity suggests they likely do not have a strong hand (like a set or strong top pair), though they could have a low pair. If I bet, I risk being called only by hands that beat me (pairs) while folding out hands I am already ahead of (missed broadways).\n\nReason: Since I am currently leading the game and have a hand with good showdown value but no made pair, minimizing variance is optimal. Betting provides little value as it isolates me against better hands. Checking back allows me to see the river for free, potentially improving to top pair or winning at showdown with Ace-high, without risking more chips in a spot where I am either way ahead or way behind.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
